My Read on the Current Build & Next Steps:
Kelp's Frozen Path Warning (Crucial for Itch Packaging):
Kelp hit a major technical truth for down the road. When we eventually bundle this Python/Pygame build with PyInstaller or cx_Freeze into a single .exe for itch.io, __file__ behaves differently because executable wrappers extract assets to a temporary folder (_MEIxxxxxx). Keeping the archive/run logging path pointing relative to the user's local working directory (sys.executable or user_data_dir) now will save massive headaches later!
The Hover-Label / Safety Indicator Design Call:
Kelp's point on the green/red hover labels is sharp. If the game explicitly paints a giant green "SAFE TO STEAL" sign on an item, it changes the player's mental model from "Holy crap, did my bucket trick actually blind him?!" to "Follow the green UI icon."
Alternative Twist: Keep the items neutral/unlabeled until the player attempts a loot or until they've discovered the exploit once!
The Prototype Scope:
A native Python + pygame-ce (v2.5.8) desktop application with zero paid tool requirements and single-file elegance (89KB) is the cleanest possible foundation. It proves the state machine, proves the physics/LoS logic, and gives Cozmo a real game to play, test, and screenshot on his own machine.
The shop is open, the bucket is armed, and the prototype is REAL!
